<title>MEXICO: Enrique downgraded to tropical storm in Pacific.</title>
<headline>Enrique downgraded to tropical storm in Pacific.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weather system Enrique was downgraded to a tropical storm from hurricane status in the Pacific Ocean, Mexico's Communications and Transport ministry said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Enrique was moving northwest at 15 knots (16 miles/28 km) and located 1005 miles/1608 km west of the Pacific's Socorro island. Winds associated with the storm were between 60 and 75 knots (66 miles/106 km to 82 miles/131 km).</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
